        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for nm-configurator",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for nm-configurator fixes the following issue\n\nUpdate to version 0.3.5.\n\nSecurity issue fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-25541: bytes: integer overflow in `BytesMut:reserve` can lead to undefined behavior and crashes\n  (bsc#1271392).\n\nOther updates and bugfixes:\n\n- Version 0.3.5:\n  * Bump `version` to v0.3.5 (#206)\n  * Bump `clap` 4.5.53 (#205)\n  * Bump `actions/checkout` to 6 (#204)\n  * Bump `nmstate` to 2.2.55 (#203)\n  * Fix for issue #198 VLAN interface renaming (#201)\n  * Bump `serde` to 1.0.228 (#196)\n  * Bump `anyhow` to 1.0.100 (#194)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
